actual_segment,predicted_segment,error_count,operational_consequence
B,C,157,Customer Segment B is assigned to Segment C. This is particularly important because B-to-C is the largest observed error pair. Segment-specific offers or retention actions could therefore be systematically misdirected.
B,A,92,Customer Segment B is assigned to Segment A. This can lead to unsuitable targeting or customer communication and may cause resources to be directed toward the wrong customer group.
A,C,88,"Customer Segment A is assigned to Segment C. Marketing or retention actions designed for Segment C may be applied to an A customer, producing less personalized engagement."
A,D,83,"Customer Segment A is assigned to Segment D. A customer may receive a substantially different priority, promotion, or engagement strategy from the one intended for their actual segment."
D,A,72,Customer Segment D is assigned to Segment A. This may cause a customer to receive a substantially different engagement or marketing treatment.
